from pathlib import Path
from html import escape as e
import json
root=Path(__file__).parent
r=json.loads((root/'requirements.json').read_text())['items']
screens=[('Homepage','index.html','Three audience cards, optional tools, short drawers, explainer module and general enquiries.'),('For clients','for-clients/','Team models, roles, practice areas, optional fee comparison, short enquiry and FAQs.'),('For consultants','for-consultants/','Optional role choice, assessment journey, earnings example, initial application and FAQs.'),('For consulting firms','for-consulting-firms/','Challenges, partnership journey, missed-project tool, short enquiry and FAQs.')]
cards=''.join(f'<a class="review-card" href="{url}"><h2>{title} ↗</h2><p>{desc}</p><span class="review-status">Ready for client review · awaiting approval</span></a>' for title,url,desc in screens)
rows=''.join(f'<tr><td>{x["id"]}</td><td><strong>{e(x["item"])}</strong><br>{e(x["question"])}</td><td>{e(x["status"])}</td><td>{e(x["owner"])}</td></tr>' for x in r)
html=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow"><title>Public website review | OptimIQ Consultus</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="site.css?v=1.2.1"></head><body><main class="review-main"><a class="text-link" href="../index.html#public-website-review">← All client review screens</a><p class="eyebrow">PUBLIC WEBSITE · PROPOSED DESIGN 1</p><h1>One connected website. Four pages to review.</h1><p>The homepage and audience journeys use the same visual system and shared form rules. Review the page layout, copy and interactions. The preview sends no enquiries, applications or messages.</p><div class="review-grid">{cards}</div><section class="review-section"><h2>What is ready for review</h2><p>Shared navigation, direct short forms, deep links, calculator confirmation and optional attachments, role selection, mobile actions, FAQs, video fallbacks and form validation. Client and firm enquiries request three required fields. Firm practice area is optional everywhere.</p><p><a href="REVIEW-TESTS.md">Verification results</a> · <a href="README.md">Developer handover</a></p></section><section class="review-section"><h2>Client assets and decisions still needed</h2><p>These items are tracked separately from screen readiness. No missing asset or proposed business assumption is treated as approved. The member portal and existing staging registration pages have not been changed.</p><table class="review-table"><thead><tr><th>Reference</th><th>Required input or decision</th><th>Status</th><th>Owner to nominate</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows}</tbody></table></section><section class="review-section"><h2>Review assumptions</h2><p>The public role label remains Consultant, matching the approved portal. The designer’s Strategy Consultant label needs confirmation. The nine practice labels are proposed public wording and require mapping to the authoritative business master. Missing guides remain hidden. The required films remain visible as review placeholders with readable overviews.</p><p>Public forms currently validate and prepare a local preview only. Production success states require durable backend receipt; verification wording appears only after an actual queued-email response. Mocked service tests do not count as a live integration test.</p></section></main></body></html>'''
(root/'review.html').write_text(html,encoding='utf-8')
print('Built public website review inventory and dependency register.')
